        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "Now I have a much clearer picture. The \"companion server\" is NOT the Paperclip Node.js server running alongside. There are actually TWO different systems:\n\n1. **Sidecar** (`SidecarClient`) — a companion Node.js server that handles filesystem/git/plugin operations. This is a separate HTTP server.\n\n2. **Sandbox Bridge** (`SandboxBridgeExecutor`) — an HTTP server that executes commands in a sandbox (either E2B or SSH-accessible machine). This is where adapter execution happens (running Claude CLI, Codex, etc.). This is the sandbox mentioned in the heartbeat/plugin-dispatch workflows.\n\n\nThe sandbox bridge itself is flexible—it can point to an E2B sandbox, a Cloudflare Container, or any self-hosted server, depending on how it's configured. So the companion server isn't necessarily in a sandbox at all; the sandbox bridge is the abstraction layer that can route to different execution environments. The `/management` endpoint for plugin installation requires filesystem access, so that operation also needs to run on the sidecar or a direct Node.js server rather than within Cloudflare itself. This means plugins execute wherever the sandbox bridge points to, not natively in Cloudflare infrastructure.",
        "type": "thinking"
      }
    ],
